==Danish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|da|non|svá}}, from {{der|da|gem-pro|*swa}}, {{m|gem-pro|*swē}}, cognate with {{cog|en|so}}, {{cog|de|so}}, {{cog|nl|zo}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|da|/ˈsɔ/|[ˈsʌ]}}, {{q|with verbs and nouns also}} {{IPA|da|/ˈsɔːˀ/|[ˈsɔˀ]}}.

====Adverb====
{{da-adv}}

# {{l|en|so}} {{q|with adjectives, to the extent (that), often with a following {{glossary|dependent clause|dependent}} result clause introduced with the conjunction {{l|da|at}}}}
# {{l|en|as}} {{q|with adjectives, introducing a comparison, the second member is introduced with the conjunction {{l|da|som}}}}
#*'''1835''', Hans Christian Andersen, ''Fyrtøiet'':
#*:Men Hunden, som sidder paa Pengekisten, har her to Øine, hvert '''saa''' stort som Rundetaarn.
#*::But the dog that sits on the money chest has two eyes, each '''as''' big as {{w|Rundetaarn}}.
# {{lb|da|dated}} {{l|en|so}}, {{l|en|like that}} {{q|with verbs}}
#*'''1876''', Holger Drachmann, ''En overkomplet'', p. 172 / https://books.google.dk/books?id=h2-8F-Y1Yy4C&pg=PA172
#*:Men det var nok ikke saa.
#*::But it probably wasn't like that.
#*Children's song, unknown origin
#*:Han sagde '''så''' og spurgte '''så''': | "Og hvor har du så hjemme?"
#*::He said '''so''' and asked '''so''': "So, where are you from?"
#: {{synonyms|da|således|sådan}}
# {{l|en|then}}, {{l|en|next}} {{q|adverb of time, temporal sequence}}
#: {{synonyms|da|derefter|derpå|herefter|herpå}}
# {{l|en|then}}, {{l|en|consequently}} {{q|adverb of causal sequence}}
#: {{synonyms|da|af den grund|altså|derfor|følgelig|således}}

